{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2837 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "7a954854adbf3cc2c9d78f77735b0b123c9fc837b069389035c91a45fab56a1a" :edb/db-before-t 2836 :edb/db-after-t 2837 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536149 50 #inst "2026-10-09T17:06:07.193Z" 13194139536149 true] [17592186114995 1145 "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{2}R_1,\n\\qquad\nR_1 := R_1+(-3)R_2.\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/assets/694b10f1d1c18f25e079e9e7cc75e9cc457ef01d0c229f006308fd667108459b.png)" 13194139536149 false] [17592186114995 1145 "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{2}R_1,\n\\qquad\nR_1 := R_1+(-3)R_2.\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080619/assets/0a034d98da82572a523d406379ab286d1af6b37820f5c2380822abf611643f83.png)" 13194139536149 true] [17592186114996 1145 "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/assets/247c0a29294e61735b969d769d8ba3794c0b5e816c3968a8db087740eeb925d8.png)" 13194139536149 false] [17592186114996 1145 "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix $A^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080619/assets/89189584fab0cbb79fb0b4ac30a81b41bfd6508de7499c111fd53fb6c0c2c928.png)" 13194139536149 true] [17592186114997 1100 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2 \\,$ and $\\, R_2 :=  R_2+(-1)R_1?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042225/assets/e607bba88cc1f15abaa45fc3cf02110243433d60259c56805515ced373054ca0.png)" 13194139536149 false] [17592186114997 1100 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2 \\,$ and $\\, R_2 :=  R_2+(-1)R_1?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080619/assets/e607bba88cc1f15abaa45fc3cf02110243433d60259c56805515ced373054ca0.png)" 13194139536149 true] [17592186115169 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386114 13194139536149 true] [17592186115169 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386121 13194139536149 true] [17592186115170 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386100 13194139536149 true] [17592186115170 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386107 13194139536149 true] [17592186115170 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386128 13194139536149 true] [17592186115171 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386135 13194139536149 true] [17592186115171 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386142 13194139536149 true] [17592186115763 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536149 true] [17592186115763 1100 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2 \\cdot 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations $R_{1}↔R_{2}$ and $R_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}R_{1}$?\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139536149 false] [17592186115763 1100 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139536149 true] [17592186115763 1145 "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"." 13194139536149 true] [17592186115764 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536149 true] [17592186115764 1100 "The inverse of the matrix $A$ is found using the row operations as shown below. What are the corresponding row operations?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536149 true] [17592186115764 1100 "The inverse of the matrix $A$ is found using the row operations as shown below. What are the corresponding row operations?\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}A & I\\end{bmatrix}|= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}___________ \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}___________; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139536149 false] [17592186115764 1145 "We write down $A$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $A$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1},\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${A}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139536149 true] [17592186386100 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386101 13194139536149 true] [17592186386100 1089 "q-131380" 13194139536149 true] [17592186386100 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536149 true] [17592186386100 1100 "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${A}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536149 true] [17592186386100 1113 #uuid "69c3d843-e9dd-52a0-9c3a-7112e0ce14b6" 13194139